; ============================================================
; UP-ERA STANCE ALIASES (platform adaptation, no donor analogue)
; The donor (UP 1.6 era) uses bare `defensive` / `no-attack` as
; AttackStance operands (9 rules in the scouting slice); DE accepts
; only stance-defensive / stance-no-attack / stance-aggressive /
; stance-stand-ground. Numeric ids from the engine registry:
; aggressive 0, defensive 1, stand-ground 2, no-attack 3.
; Aliasing (rather than rewriting 9 authenticated rule bodies)
; preserves 244/244 positional equivalence; the engine receives
; the identical integer. If runtime disproves numeric acceptance,
; fall back to rewriting the 9 rules with stance-* names.
; ============================================================
(defconst defensive 1)
(defconst no-attack 3)
